@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-rental-periods-are-half-open-whole-day-utc-intervals
+type: decision-log
+title: "Rental periods are half-open whole-day UTC intervals"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+School rules 2 and 3: times are UTC ISO-8601, and a rental covers whole days only. A period starts at
+midnight UTC and ends at the start of the day after its last day. Rule 4 forbids overlapping bookings of
+the same item.
+
+## Decision
+
+A period is the half-open interval `[start, end)`. Its price is `dailyPrice` times the number of days,
+where the number of days is `(end - start) / 24h`. A period must have `end` strictly after `start`.
+Two periods overlap when each starts before the other ends. A period may therefore begin on the day
+another one ends.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Back-to-back rentals of the same board are allowed without a gap day.
+- Pricing is a pure integer multiplication, so the total stays in whole euro cents (rule 1).
+- Cancellation (not implemented yet) will reuse the same period values.
diff --git a/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-002-rental-input-is-validated-strictly-at-the-service-boundary.md b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-002-rental-input-is-validated-strictly-at-the-service-boundary.md
