+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-002-rental-input-is-validated-strictly-at-the-service-boundary.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+---
+id: dl-002-rental-input-is-validated-strictly-at-the-service-boundary
+type: decision-log
+title: "Rental input is validated strictly at the service boundary"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The rental service is the entry point for the booking desk. Its callers are not trusted to pass
+well-formed values, and a wrong date or price would silently produce a wrong charge.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Item: `id` is a non-empty string and unique within the service; `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'`;
+  `dailyPrice` is a non-negative safe integer of euro cents (zero is accepted).
+- Time: a value is accepted only when it has the form `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00Z`, optionally with
+  `.000` milliseconds, and names an existing calendar day. Offsets such as `+02:00`, local-time
+  strings, and times that are not midnight are refused.
+- Errors are thrown as `Error` with a message that names the offending field.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Callers must send UTC midnight strings; the service does not convert other time zones.
+- Only ISO strings are accepted, so the output echoes the input period unchanged.
