@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-rental-bookings-use-deterministic-in-memory-ids
+type: decision-log
+title: "Rental bookings use deterministic in-memory ids"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The module keeps everything in memory for now. The determinism directive forbids wall-clock time and
+randomness in code paths that build state, and tests must not depend on either.
+
+## Decision
+
+Each service numbers its bookings from a counter it owns: `booking-1`, `booking-2`, and so on. Bookings
+are kept in insertion order. Each `createRentalService()` call starts its own counter and its own store.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Given the same sequence of calls, ids and results are identical, so tests need no mocks.
+- Ids are unique only within one service instance. A persistent store will need a different scheme,
+  to be decided with that store.
