+---
+id: task-001-rental-module-basics-for-booking-desk
+type: task
+title: "Rental module basics for booking desk"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Add the basics of a rental module to the booking desk: `createRentalService()`, exported from
+`src/index.ts`, with `addEquipment`, `quote` and `book`, following the school's five rules. Cancellations
+are out of scope for now.
+
+## Done
+
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: 24 tests written first and seen failing (module missing), then passing against
+  the implementation. They cover happy paths and error paths for each method, back-to-back and overlapping
+  periods, unknown items, invalid times, and service isolation.
+- `src/index.ts`: the service, in memory, with doc comments on every export.
+- `README.md`: a short section describing the module and its period rules.
+- Design choices are recorded in `dl-001` to `dl-004`.
+
+## Checks
+
+- `npm test` (`node --test`): 24 of 24 pass.
+- `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` with a temporary TypeScript 5 install (not added to the project): no errors.
+
+## Open points
+
+- The project has no TypeScript or test dependency declared, so the tests run on Node's built-in type
+  stripping (Node 22.23 here). Importing `../src/index.ts` with a `.ts` extension is what allows that.
+- No coverage threshold is declared, so none is enforced.
+- Rule 5 (cancellation refunds) is not implemented, as requested.
